<title>RUSSIA: Russia Nizhnetagilsk 96 loss 566 bln rbls.</title>
<headline>Russia Nizhnetagilsk 96 loss 566 bln rbls.</headline>
<dateline>YEKATERINBURG, Russia 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31:</p>
<p>		(figures in billion roubles unless specified)</p>
<p>					  1996			 1995</p>
<p> Net sales			  7,695.02		  6,464.39</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			15.53		    987.88</p>
<p> Net loss			    -566.30		     n/a</p>
<p> Accounts receivable	    1,374.04		  1,050.89</p>
<p> Accounts payable		 3,791.94		  1,896.22</p>
<p> Dividends</p>
<p>  ordinary				0			8 rbls</p>
<p> Exports				$486.5 million		   n/a</p>
<p> Rolled iron production	4,055,600 T	     3,872,300 T</p>
<p> Cast iron production	    352,700 T		 560,400 T</p>
<p>NOTES - Full name AO Nizhnetagilsky Metallurgichesky Kombinat (Nizhnetagilsk Metal in English).</p>
<p>Figures to Russian accruals accounting standards.</p>
<p>Ordinary shares have a face value of 1,000 roubles.</p>
<p>The company's authorised capital is 1.03 billion roubles. Its biggest shareholders are AOZT Grin with 15.92 percent, Century Holding Ltd with 10 percent, Duferko Holding Ltd with 10 percent and TOO Interural with 8.11 percent.</p>
<p>The company decided in May to increase its authorised capital to 2.07 trillion roubles by issuing 1.03 billion ordinary shares.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
